{"id":"aacfe95320c32726","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-df-cauchyseq.md","title":"Cauchy Sequence","display":"df-cauchyseq — Cauchy Sequence","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-cauchyseq","aliases":["58-df-cauchyseq"],"display":"df-cauchyseq — Cauchy Sequence","depends_on":["[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-cauchyseq"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-cauchyseq</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-cauchyseq — Cauchy Sequence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s,d\\in V\">\\(s,d\\in V\\)</span> (sequence candidate and metric)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (metric-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CauchySeq}_d\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{CauchySeq}_d\\subseteq V\\)</span> (Cauchy-sequence predicate for the metric <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\">\\(d\\)</span>, defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cauchyseq} \\vdash \\mathrm{CauchySeq}_d(s) \\leftrightarrow \\exists X\\in V\\;\\left(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land s\\in X^\\omega\\land\\forall \\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists N \\in \\omega\\;\\forall m,n\\in\\omega\\;((m\\geq N \\land n\\geq N) \\to d(s(m),s(n))&lt;\\varepsilon)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cauchyseq} \\vdash \\mathrm{CauchySeq}_d(s) \\leftrightarrow \\exists X\\in V\\;\\left(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land s\\in X^\\omega\\land\\forall \\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists N \\in \\omega\\;\\forall m,n\\in\\omega\\;((m\\geq N \\land n\\geq N) \\to d(s(m),s(n))&lt;\\varepsilon)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Symbol\">[Symbol]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>CauchySeq</code>: Cauchy sequence</li>\n<li><code>MetricSpace</code>: Metric space</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The carrier is existentially recovered from the metric-space predicate, so the domain-indexed notation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CauchySeq}_d\">\\(\\mathrm{CauchySeq}_d\\)</span> has no free hidden carrier parameter.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Symbol","text":"[Symbol]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2$ (metric-space predicate, see [[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"s,d\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CauchySeq}_d\\subseteq V","display":false},{"tex":"d","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cauchyseq} \\vdash \\mathrm{CauchySeq}_d(s) \\leftrightarrow \\exists X\\in V\\;\\left(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land s\\in X^\\omega\\land\\forall \\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\exists N \\in \\omega\\;\\forall m,n\\in\\omega\\;((m\\geq N \\land n\\geq N) \\to d(s(m),s(n))<\\varepsilon)\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CauchySeq}_d","display":false}],"bytes":1108,"backlinks":[{"id":"3a32009d673e1bd4","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"1746581a68e233ce","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"a11585cba9c21cfd","anchor":"ref-328","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-df-cauchyseq]]"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-256","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-cauchyseq.md|58-df-cauchyseq]]（batch08）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-22","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-df-def-operator.md]]\n[[58-df-l-hierarchy.md]]\n[[58-df-p-name.md]]\n[[58-df-aleph.md]]\n[[58-df-antichain.md]]\n[[58-df-baire-property.md]]\n[[58-df-beth-function.md]]\n[[58-df-bijective.md]]\n[[58-df-borel.md]]\n[[58-df-bounded.md]]\n[[58-df-branch.md]]\n[[58-df-cardinal.md]]\n[[58-df-cardinaladd.md]]\n[[58-df-cardinalclass.md]]\n[[58-df-cardinalexpp.md]]\n[[58-df-cardinality.md]]\n[[58-df-cardinalmul.md]]\n[[58-df-cartesian.md]]\n[[58-df-cauchy.md]]\n[[58-df-cauchyseq.md]]\n[[58-df-ch.md]]\n[[58-df-chain.md]]\n[[58-df-closed.md]]\n[[58-df-club-filter.md]]\n[[58-df-club.md]]\n[[58-df-cofinality.md]]\n[[58-df-compatible.md]]\n[[58-df-constructible-universe.md]]\n[[58-df-continuous.md]]\n[[58-df-continuum.md]]\n[[58-df-countable.md]]\n[[58-df-critical-point.md]]\n[[58-df-ctm.md]]\n[[58-df-dedekind-cut.md]]\n[[58-df-dense.md]]\n[[58-df-diamond.md]]\n[[58-df-diff.md]]\n[[58-df-disjoint.md]]\n[[58-df-domain.md]]\n[[58-df-dual-ideal.md]]\n